      "knowledge_point": "The Domain of a Function Containing Exponential, Logarithmic, and Trigonometric Functions",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.",
